language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_050_diamond_free: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Find a simple undirected graph on N vertices, with no loops, that is diamond-free: no four vertices have at least five edges between them, so the graph has no diamond as an induced subgraph. The degrees d_1 >= d_2 >= ... >= d_N are non-increasing, each degree is greater than zero and divisible by 3, and the sum of the degrees is divisible by 12 (so the number of edges is divisible by 6).
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_050_diamond_free.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_050_diamond_free.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_050_diamond_free_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_050_diamond_free.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_050_diamond_free_1.param -run-solver

$ N: number of vertices
given N : int(1..)

$ matrix_[u,v]: vertices u and v are adjacent (indices 1-based; named matrix_ because matrix is an Essence' word)
find matrix_ : matrix indexed by [int(1..N), int(1..N)] of bool
$ deg[u]: degree of vertex u, the number of vertices adjacent to u (auxiliary, a function of matrix_)
find deg : matrix indexed by [int(1..N)] of int(0..N-1)

branching on [matrix_]
such that
$ the graph is simple: no vertex is adjacent to itself
forAll u : int(1..N) . (!matrix_[u,u]),
$ the graph is undirected: adjacency is symmetric
forAll u : int(1..N) . forAll v : int(1..N) . (matrix_[u,v] = matrix_[v,u]),
$ deg[u] is the number of vertices adjacent to u
forAll u : int(1..N) . (deg[u] = (sum v : int(1..N) . toInt(matrix_[u,v]))),
$ the degrees are listed in non-increasing order, d_u >= d_(u+1)
forAll u : int(1..N-1) . (deg[u] >= deg[u+1]),
$ each degree is greater than zero and divisible by 3
forAll u : int(1..N) . (deg[u] > 0 /\ deg[u] % 3 = 0),
$ the sum of the degrees is divisible by 12
(sum u : int(1..N) . deg[u]) % 12 = 0,
$ diamond-free: among any four vertices there are at most four edges
forAll a : int(1..N) . forAll b : int(a+1..N) . forAll c : int(b+1..N) . forAll d : int(c+1..N) . ((toInt(matrix_[a,b]) + toInt(matrix_[a,c]) + toInt(matrix_[a,d]) + toInt(matrix_[b,c]) + toInt(matrix_[b,d]) + toInt(matrix_[c,d])) <= 4)
